window.JESTBOX_JOKES["en-IN"].push(...[[["characters"],"At the apartment lift, the watchman taped up a notice saying the lift was on a diet.\nResidents were told to travel one floor at a time to help it lose weight.\nSomeone asked whether the stairs were its personal trainer."],[["characters"],"The building secretary introduced a digital complaint register.\nThe first complaint said the QR code was blocking the notice board.\nThe secretary closed it as a successful paperless resolution."],[["characters"],"A resident complained that the corridor light switched off too quickly.\nThe electrician adjusted the timer and asked him to walk with purpose.\nThe resident said he had finally found a building that judged his pace."],[["characters"],"The society gardener asked for a raise because the plants were getting all the attention.\nThe committee offered him a title: Director of Leaf Affairs.\nHe accepted, then submitted a pruning budget with executive benefits."],[["characters"],"During the fire drill, one resident brought his pressure cooker downstairs.\nHe said the whistle was the only alarm he trusted.\nThe safety officer asked him to leave the lunch plan out of the evacuation plan."],[["characters"],"The parking committee painted fresh numbers on every slot.\nOne resident parked between two lines and called it a flexible arrangement.\nThe committee gave him a map and labelled the space “creative writing”."],[["characters"],"A neighbour installed a doorbell that played classical music.\nThe delivery agent waited through the entire raga before ringing again.\nThe owner complained that nobody respected the short version of the concert."],[["characters"],"The treasurer announced that the annual accounts were now available online.\nA resident asked for a printed copy because his phone had no patience for PDFs.\nThe treasurer said the printer was also waiting for the audit to finish."],[["characters"],"At the water-tank inspection, everyone blamed the upstairs flat.\nThe plumber found a leaking tap in the committee office.\nThe committee minutes recorded the discovery as “a collective learning opportunity”."],[["characters"],"The residents voted to make the terrace a quiet zone.\nBy evening, three people had booked it for yoga, two for karaoke and one for a pressure-washer demo.\nThe secretary renamed it the society’s multipurpose silence centre."],[["characters"],"The society secretary announced that the lift would be repaired by Monday.\nThe watchman asked which Monday; the secretary said, “The one after the contractor arrives.”\nThe lift has now been promoted to the building's permanent staircase."],[["characters"],"A wedding photographer asked everyone to smile naturally.\nThe groom's uncle began giving instructions on how to smile in three generations.\nThe photographer saved the lecture as the evening's longest exposure."],[["characters"],"The cricket umpire at the office picnic called a meeting to review the boundary.\nThe ball had already landed in the next society, where residents demanded a visitor pass.\nThe match ended with a diplomatic exchange of the ball."],[["characters"],"The school principal asked the class monitor to maintain silence.\nThe monitor raised a hand and requested permission to announce the silence rules.\nThe class learned that administration can be louder than the problem."],[["characters"],"The train announcer apologised for a delay and promised an update shortly.\nA passenger asked whether “shortly” was measured in minutes or railway seasons.\nThe platform clock declined to be quoted."],[["characters"],"The building watchman announced that the parcel register was now fully digital.\nResidents still had to sign a paper book to collect each delivery.\nHe called it a hybrid system: the parcel travels online, the signature travels by pen."],[["characters"],"The wedding caterer promised a live counter with instant service.\nThe queue moved so slowly that the chef had time to learn everyone's names.\nBy dessert, he was greeting customers like old school friends."],[["characters"],"The cricket commentator at the office tournament described every ball dramatically.\nWhen the batter missed, he announced a strategic pause in the scoring department.\nThe scorer asked him to commentate on the scoreboard instead."],[["characters"],"The school bus driver asked the children to keep the aisle clear.\nOne child moved his bag but left his collection of toy cars in the middle.\nThe driver declared it a miniature traffic problem."],[["characters"],"The apartment electrician labelled every switch in the common area.\nOne resident asked which switch controlled the committee's decisions.\nThe electrician pointed to the one marked “power supply” and walked away."],[["characters"], "The detective in the school play questioned a missing lunchbox.\nThe suspect was a magician who kept pulling sandwiches from his hat.\nThe audience solved the mystery when the magician asked for ketchup."],[["characters"], "A superhero promised to protect the city from every inconvenience.\nA resident asked him to fix the lift that stopped between floors.\nHe flew away and returned with a handwritten apology from the building committee."],[["characters"], "The pirate captain demanded a map to buried treasure.\nHis first mate handed him the office cafeteria menu.\n“Every Friday,” the mate explained, “the dessert disappears without a trace.”"],[["characters"], "The robot joined a family game night and learned charades.\nIt acted out “washing machine” by spinning in place.\nThe family guessed “home appliance having a software update.”"],[["characters"], "The detective interviewed a parrot that had witnessed the theft.\nThe bird repeated the same phrase whenever asked for details.\nThe detective closed the case: the parrot had clearly been trained by the press office."],[["characters"],"At the school annual day, the tuition teacher volunteered to handle a wedding buffet.\nThey created a one-way system near the gulab jamun.\nThe dessert counter became the busiest traffic junction in town. The tuition teacher added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"],"At the school annual day, the tuition teacher volunteered to handle a lift breakdown.\nThey called for calm and formed a subcommittee.\nThe lift reached the floor before the subcommittee reached a decision. The tuition teacher added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"],"At the school annual day, the tuition teacher volunteered to handle a society clean-up.\nThey distributed gloves and motivational speeches.\nThe dustbin was the only member who completed the task. The tuition teacher added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"],"At the school annual day, the tuition teacher volunteered to handle a family photo.\nThey asked everyone to look natural.\nThe photographer captured twelve poses and one genuine blink. The tuition teacher added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"],"At the school annual day, the tuition teacher volunteered to handle a budget discussion.\nThey promised a transparent calculation.\nThe calculator displayed the total and immediately went into hiding. The tuition teacher added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"],"At a rainy evening, the auto driver volunteered to handle a power cut.\nThey appointed the inverter as chief guest.\nThe inverter refused to speak until the fan was switched on. The auto driver added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"],"At a rainy evening, the auto driver volunteered to handle a surprise downpour.\nThey declared the event officially indoors.\nThe clouds asked who had approved the venue change. The auto driver added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"],"At a rainy evening, the auto driver volunteered to handle a missing tiffin.\nThey launched a full investigation before lunch.\nThe evidence pointed to the person holding the empty dabba. The auto driver added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"],"At a rainy evening, the auto driver volunteered to handle a delayed train.\nThey announced a revised timetable with confidence.\nThe timetable requested a transfer to a less dramatic route. The auto driver added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"],"At a rainy evening, the auto driver volunteered to handle a cricket final.\nThey introduced a committee to inspect the boundary.\nThe ball crossed it while the committee was choosing a chairperson. The auto driver added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"], "The museum guide called a suit of armour completely fearless.\nA child asked whether it had ever faced a washing machine.\nThe guide admitted even brave knights feared delicate-care labels."],[["characters"], "A space explorer messaged home about finding intelligent life.\nMission control asked for proof.\nThe explorer replied, “The planet has a help desk, and it answered on the first call.”"],[["characters"], "The magician promised to make a chair disappear.\nHe covered it with a cloth and pulled the cloth away.\nThe chair was gone; the stage manager asked who had moved the props."],[["characters"], "A parrot applied for a receptionist job.\nThe manager asked whether it could keep conversations confidential.\nThe parrot repeated the question to the entire waiting room."],[["characters"], "The time traveller arrived late to a history lecture.\nThe professor asked what had delayed him.\nHe said, “The past has roadworks too.”"],[["characters"],"At the office tea break, the chai vendor volunteered to handle a power cut.\nThey appointed the inverter as chief guest.\nThe inverter refused to speak until the fan was switched on. The chai vendor added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"],"At the office tea break, the chai vendor volunteered to handle a surprise downpour.\nThey declared the event officially indoors.\nThe clouds asked who had approved the venue change. The chai vendor added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"],"At the office tea break, the chai vendor volunteered to handle a missing tiffin.\nThey launched a full investigation before lunch.\nThe evidence pointed to the person holding the empty dabba. The chai vendor added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"],"At the office tea break, the chai vendor volunteered to handle a delayed train.\nThey announced a revised timetable with confidence.\nThe timetable requested a transfer to a less dramatic route. The chai vendor added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"],"At the office tea break, the chai vendor volunteered to handle a cricket final.\nThey introduced a committee to inspect the boundary.\nThe ball crossed it while the committee was choosing a chairperson. The chai vendor added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"], "The colony secretary announced a contest for the neatest balcony.\nThe watchman entered the staircase instead.\n“Madam, everyone throws the balcony mess downstairs,” he explained.\nThe secretary quietly cancelled the judging round."],[["characters"], "A retired teacher joined the family quiz and insisted on marking every answer.\nHis grandson asked, “Can we appeal?”\n“Certainly,” said the teacher.\nThe child appealed the marks, not the questions."],[["characters"], "The local magician promised to make a sofa disappear.\nHe covered it with a sheet, clapped twice, and lifted the cloth.\nThe sofa was still there.\nThe family had vanished to avoid helping him move it."],[["characters"], "A wedding photographer told the groom, “Give me a natural smile.”\nThe groom asked whether he had seen the catering bill.\nThe photographer lowered the camera.\n“Fair point. Let us try a financially realistic expression.”"],[["characters"], "The neighbourhood electrician was invited to a housewarming.\nThe host asked him for a blessing.\n“May every connection in this house be secure,” he said, touching the switchboard.\nThe inverter beeped in agreement."],[["characters"], "A traffic constable visited a school career day.\nA child asked what the hardest part of his job was.\n“Explaining a U-turn,” he said.\n“People understand the sign; it is their plans that refuse to turn.”"],[["characters"], "The society gardener entered the residents’ meeting carrying a tiny plant.\n“This one is for the committee,” he announced.\n“It grows slowly, needs regular attention, and gets blamed when the weather changes.”\nNobody volunteered to take it home."],[["characters"], "A radio host asked a local poet for a two-line introduction.\nThe poet delivered twelve lines.\n“We only have ten seconds,” the host whispered.\n“Then broadcast the silence,” said the poet. “It is my shortest poem.”"],[["characters"], "A bus conductor was asked why he never argued with passengers about change.\n“I keep exact change,” he said.\n“It is the only relationship in this city where both sides agree on the amount.”\nThe next passenger asked for a discount."],[["characters"], "A tailor displayed a sign promising a perfect fit.\nA customer returned with a shirt that was too tight.\nThe tailor measured him again.\n“The shirt is perfect. Your weekend snacks have changed the requirements.”"],[["characters"],"At a neighbourhood match, the cricket umpire volunteered to handle a wedding buffet.\nThey created a one-way system near the gulab jamun.\nThe dessert counter became the busiest traffic junction in town. The cricket umpire added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"],"At a neighbourhood match, the cricket umpire volunteered to handle a lift breakdown.\nThey called for calm and formed a subcommittee.\nThe lift reached the floor before the subcommittee reached a decision. The cricket umpire added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"],"At a neighbourhood match, the cricket umpire volunteered to handle a society clean-up.\nThey distributed gloves and motivational speeches.\nThe dustbin was the only member who completed the task. The cricket umpire added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"],"At a neighbourhood match, the cricket umpire volunteered to handle a family photo.\nThey asked everyone to look natural.\nThe photographer captured twelve poses and one genuine blink. The cricket umpire added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"],"At a neighbourhood match, the cricket umpire volunteered to handle a budget discussion.\nThey promised a transparent calculation.\nThe calculator displayed the total and immediately went into hiding. The cricket umpire added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"],"At the society festival, the building watchman volunteered to handle a power cut.\nThey appointed the inverter as chief guest.\nThe inverter refused to speak until the fan was switched on. The building watchman added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"],"At the society festival, the building watchman volunteered to handle a surprise downpour.\nThey declared the event officially indoors.\nThe clouds asked who had approved the venue change. The building watchman added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"],"At the society festival, the building watchman volunteered to handle a missing tiffin.\nThey launched a full investigation before lunch.\nThe evidence pointed to the person holding the empty dabba. The building watchman added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"],"At the society festival, the building watchman volunteered to handle a delayed train.\nThey announced a revised timetable with confidence.\nThe timetable requested a transfer to a less dramatic route. The building watchman added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"],"At the society festival, the building watchman volunteered to handle a cricket final.\nThey introduced a committee to inspect the boundary.\nThe ball crossed it while the committee was choosing a chairperson. The building watchman added it to the next agenda."],[["characters"], "The bank clerk volunteered to organise the office farewell.\nHe made a list of contributions, expenses, and pending dues.\nThe retiring manager asked whether the farewell would be emotional.\n“Certainly,” said the clerk. “Especially when I show everyone the balance.”"],[["characters"], "A local train announcer was invited to a birthday party.\nThe host asked him to announce the cake cutting.\nHe used the platform voice: “The cake is arriving on platform one.”\nHalf the guests formed a queue and checked their tickets."],[["characters"], "A street magician offered free tricks outside a shopping mall.\nA child asked him to make the shopping bill disappear.\nThe magician tried three times, then returned the bill.\n“Sorry,” he said. “That belongs to a much more expensive magician.”"],[["characters"], "The society watchman reported a suspicious package near the gate.\nThe committee rushed down and surrounded it.\nIt turned out to be the secretary's lunchbox.\nThe watchman apologised; the secretary asked him to guard it until tea."],[["characters"], "A cricket umpire was asked to settle an argument at a family picnic.\nTwo cousins insisted they had caught the same falling mango.\nThe umpire checked the ground and declared it a boundary catch.\nThe mango was awarded to the squirrel, who had already left the venue."],[["characters"], "A wedding caterer promised a separate counter for every dietary preference.\nThe groom asked where the ordinary food would be served.\nThe caterer pointed to a tiny table and said, “That is the nostalgia counter.”\nThe groom's uncle booked it for the entire family."],[["characters"], "A school bus driver was praised for always arriving on time.\nHe thanked the parent and showed his secret.\n“I leave early,” he said. “Then I spend twenty minutes waiting outside the school.”\nThe parent replied, “That explains why the children think school opens at dawn.”"],[["characters"], "The colony gardener asked residents not to walk on the new grass.\nA resident pointed out that the grass was barely visible.\n“Exactly,” said the gardener. “I am protecting its privacy until it grows confident.”\nThe committee added a privacy fence to the maintenance budget."],[["characters"], "A photographer asked a family to stand in height order.\nThe tallest uncle moved to the back and complained.\nThe photographer said, “This is not a ranking; it is a composition.”\nThe uncle replied, “Then compose me near the snacks.”"],[["characters"], "The neighbourhood dentist put up a sign saying “Walk-ins welcome.”\nA man walked in, looked at the chair, and walked straight out.\nThe receptionist asked whether he needed an appointment.\n“No,” he said. “I was checking whether the sign also treats fear.”"],[["characters"], "A delivery rider called the customer to confirm the address.\nThe customer gave three landmarks and said the building was easy to find.\nThe rider replied, “I have found the building.”\n“Then why are you asking?” said the customer.\n“I am trying to find the entrance you call easy,” said the rider."],[["characters"], "The local tailor offered express alterations for a small extra fee.\nA customer asked whether he could shorten a trouser in ten minutes.\n“Of course,” said the tailor. “But the queue will need a calendar.”\nThe customer chose the regular service and called it a long-term investment."],[["characters"], "A retired librarian joined a quiz show as a contestant.\nThe host asked for his strongest subject.\n“Silence,” he replied.\nThe host asked for an example, and the librarian won the round without answering."],[["characters"], "A traffic constable stopped a scooter carrying three people and a large plant.\nHe asked where they were taking the plant.\n“To a family function,” said the rider.\nThe constable pointed to the helmet and said, “At least the plant has proper head protection.”"],[["characters"], "The colony electrician arrived to inspect a flickering tube light.\nHe changed the starter and waited for it to glow steadily.\nThe resident asked whether the repair was guaranteed.\n“Absolutely,” he said. “If it flickers again, you will know exactly where to find me.”"],[["characters"], "A street-food vendor introduced a loyalty card for regular customers.\nAfter ten visits, customers would receive one free plate.\nA regular asked whether the card could be stamped retroactively.\nThe vendor said, “Yes, but the free plate will also be served retroactively.”"],[["characters"], "The office peon was asked to deliver an urgent file to the director.\nHe returned with the file and a note.\nThe director had written, “Please send this through the proper channel.”\nThe peon said, “Sir, I am the channel. The file is now back at the starting point.”"],[["characters"], "A local music teacher asked the student to practise scales every morning.\nThe student said the neighbours complained about the noise.\nThe teacher suggested practising softly.\nThe student returned next week and said, “Now the neighbours complain that I am not improving loudly enough.”"],[["characters"], "A building manager announced a lift maintenance window from ten to noon.\nAt ten, residents gathered in the lobby and asked when it would start.\nThe manager pointed to the notice and said, “It has started.”\nOne resident asked, “Then why is the lift still here?”"],[["characters"], "The wedding DJ asked the bride's grandfather for a song request.\nHe requested the sound of the pressure cooker whistle.\nThe DJ laughed, thinking it was a joke.\nGrandfather said, “Play it at seven tomorrow; the whole family knows the steps.”"],[["characters"], "At the railway platform, the announcer was asked to explain a delayed train.\nHe checked the board and said, \"The train is arriving shortly.\"\nA passenger asked, \"How shortly?\"\nHe replied, \"Shortly enough for you to miss the next announcement.\""],[["characters"], "The bank cashier became the society treasurer for one month.\nHe insisted every contribution arrive with a receipt and two witnesses.\nWhen the committee asked for the balance, he showed them the empty tea fund.\n\"That,\" he said, \"is the only account nobody disputes.\""],[["characters"], "A wedding photographer told the family to act candidly.\nThe uncle immediately pretended to receive an urgent phone call.\nThe aunt pretended not to notice him pretending.\nThe photographer finally said, \"Wonderful—now please pretend this is the first take.\""],[["characters"], "The electrician arrived to fix a flickering tube light.\nThe landlord asked whether the problem was serious.\n\"Only when you switch it on,\" the electrician said.\nThe landlord nodded: \"Then let's keep it off until the rent is due.\""],[["characters"], "A magician performed a disappearing coin trick at a tea stall.\nThe stall owner watched closely and asked for the secret.\nThe magician whispered, \"Practice.\"\nThe owner replied, \"I practise every day; my customers disappear before paying.\""],[["characters"], "The bus conductor announced that exact change would make everyone's journey smoother.\nA passenger handed him a handful of coins and asked for a discount.\nThe conductor counted them twice.\n\"Your change is exact,\" he said, \"but your bargaining is travelling without a ticket.\""],[["characters"], "The school principal invited a stand-up comedian for annual day.\nThe comedian asked whether the students were allowed to laugh.\n\"Of course,\" said the principal, \"but only after the chief guest finishes.\"\nThe comedian moved his entire set to the interval."],[["characters"], "A chef entered a cooking contest with a pressure cooker.\nThe judge asked what made the dish special.\n\"Time management,\" said the chef.\n\"Everyone else is still chopping; my dinner has already resigned from the kitchen.\""],[["characters"], "The watch repairer was asked why a wall clock always ran late.\nHe opened the back and studied the mechanism.\n\"Your clock is not slow,\" he said, \"it is avoiding your appointments.\"\nThe customer asked for a warranty; the repairer offered a calendar."],[["characters"], "A traffic constable stopped a man who had crossed on a red signal.\nThe man said he was following the crowd.\nThe constable pointed to the empty road.\n\"Then why did you cross alone?\"\n\"Because the crowd had better judgement,\" the man admitted."],[["characters"], "The librarian asked a noisy visitor to keep his voice down.\nThe visitor whispered that he was only discussing a thriller.\n\"Please discuss it silently,\" she said.\n\"Even the book's suspense is trying to concentrate.\""],[["characters"], "An interior designer showed a client a minimalist living room.\nThe client looked around and asked where the furniture was.\n\"Minimalism,\" said the designer, \"is about making space.\"\nThe client smiled: \"Excellent. My budget has been doing that for months.\""],[["characters"], "The cricket umpire was asked how he stayed calm during a heated match.\n\"I never take sides,\" he said.\nA player protested, \"You gave me out!\"\n\"That was not taking sides,\" replied the umpire, \"that was taking attendance.\""],[["characters"], "A dentist told his patient to stop eating sweets at midnight.\nThe patient asked whether one small piece would matter.\n\"Your teeth won't know the time,\" said the dentist.\n\"Neither will my wallet,\" the patient sighed, \"after this consultation.\""],[["characters"], "The building watchman reported that the lift had stopped between floors.\nThe committee asked who was responsible.\n\"Everyone,\" he said, \"because everybody pressed a different button.\"\nThe secretary called an emergency meeting to decide which floor to blame."],[["city"], "A tailor promised to finish the suit by Friday.\nThe customer asked whether that meant this Friday or next Friday.\nThe tailor measured the sleeve thoughtfully.\n\"That depends,\" he said, \"on how quickly you stop asking for updates.\""],[["city"], "The radio jockey asked listeners to share their biggest achievement.\nOne caller said he had finally cleaned his inbox.\nThe jockey asked how many unread messages remained.\n\"Three,\" said the caller, \"but they are from my family, so they are permanent.\""],[["city"], "A plumber inspected a tap that dripped all night.\nThe homeowner asked if it could be fixed without replacing anything.\n\"Certainly,\" said the plumber, \"we can replace your expectation of silence.\"\nThen he handed over a quote for a new tap."],[["city"], "The wedding caterer announced that the dessert counter was closing.\nOne guest asked for just one more gulab jamun.\nThe caterer pointed to the empty tray.\n\"Sir, the sweets have already attended their own farewell.\""],[["city"], "An insurance agent explained the policy in careful detail.\nThe customer asked what was not covered.\nThe agent paused and said, \"Your optimism.\"\nThe customer signed immediately: \"Good, I had stopped relying on that.\""],[["city"], "The photographer asked a group of cousins to stand in a straight line.\nThey arranged themselves by height, age, and family seniority.\nThe youngest cousin stepped out and said, \"I refuse to be ranked.\"\nThe photographer captured the first genuinely candid moment of the day."],[["city"], "A mechanic listened to a scooter engine and diagnosed a loose part.\nThe owner asked whether it was dangerous.\n\"Not if you enjoy surprise percussion,\" said the mechanic.\nThe scooter started with a beat that made the owner request a music licence."],[["city"], "The office receptionist asked a visitor whom he wished to meet.\nHe said, \"The person who makes decisions.\"\nShe checked the directory and replied, \"That position is currently vacant.\"\nHe asked when it would be filled.\n\"When someone decides,\" she said."],[["city"], "A barber asked his customer how short he wanted the haircut.\nThe customer said, \"Just enough to look responsible.\"\nThe barber studied his face in the mirror.\n\"Hair I can manage,\" he said, \"but that is a larger makeover.\""],[["city"], "The museum guide explained that an old telephone once connected people instantly.\nA teenager asked why anyone would need such a thing.\nThe guide said, \"To speak without sending a screenshot to the whole group.\"\nThe teenager stared at the phone as if it were ancient magic."],[["city"], "The city bus conductor announced that the route had changed because of road repairs.\nA passenger asked where the new route ended.\n“Wherever the traffic allows,” he said, collecting the exact fare."],[["city"], "A street vendor put a sign beside his cart: “Fresh ideas served here.”\nA customer asked for one with extra chutney.\nThe vendor pointed to the menu and said, “That innovation costs five rupees more.”"],[["city"], "The municipal office introduced an online queue for property questions.\nA resident booked a slot and arrived ten minutes early.\nThe screen welcomed him with: “You are number 84 in the virtual queue.”"],[["city"], "A cab driver asked a passenger whether he preferred the fastest route or the shortest one.\nThe passenger chose the fastest.\nThe driver nodded and opened a discussion about traffic psychology."],[["city"], "At the railway station, a traveller asked why the platform display kept changing.\nThe attendant said the train was punctual in spirit.\n“Only its location is still being negotiated,” he added."],[["city"], "A shopkeeper in the market installed a digital weighing scale.\nThe first customer asked whether it was accurate.\n“Absolutely,” said the shopkeeper, “it even tells me when my old scale was optimistic.”"],[["city"], "The apartment delivery rider called to say he was at the gate.\nThe resident asked which gate, because the complex had six.\n“I'm at the one with the longest security conversation,” came the reply."],[["city"], "A local barber displayed a board reading “New look, new life.”\nA customer asked if the haircut included a career upgrade.\nThe barber said, “That package is handled by the salon next door.”"],[["city"], "The city library started a late-return reminder service.\nOne reader received a message saying his book was overdue by 43 days.\nHe replied, “Please tell the book I am still thinking about the ending.”"],[["city"], "A traffic volunteer asked a motorist why he had stopped beyond the line.\nThe motorist said the signal changed before he could finish braking.\nThe volunteer replied, “Then let us both finish this conversation after the next green.”"],[["city"], "A neighbourhood café added QR codes to every table.\nA customer scanned one and found the menu, bill, feedback form and Wi-Fi password.\nHe asked where the coffee was; the waiter said, “That still arrives physically.”"],[["city"], "A tailor near the bus depot promised a shirt by the evening.\nThe customer returned at closing time to check.\nThe tailor said, “The shirt is ready; the evening is running late.”"],[["city"], "A street musician asked passers-by to request a song.\nOne commuter requested something that could make the traffic move.\nThe musician played a cheerful tune, and three pedestrians started walking faster."],[["city"], "The city park installed a board asking visitors not to feed the pigeons.\nA man read it, put away his snack and sighed.\n“The only residents here who ignore notices are the ones who can fly,” he said."],[["city"], "A customer complained that the local internet café was too slow.\nThe owner explained that the connection was on a limited plan.\nThe customer asked whether the plan also limited the speed of apologies."],[["city"], "At the vegetable market, a shopper asked for the freshest tomatoes.\nThe vendor pointed to a crate and said they had arrived that morning.\nThe shopper replied, “So have I; let's compare our energy levels.”"],[["city"], "A parking attendant handed a driver a token with a large number printed on it.\nThe driver asked whether it was his parking slot.\n“No,” said the attendant, “it's how many minutes we expect you to search for one.”"],[["city"], "The neighbourhood gym advertised a “traffic-free morning workout.”\nA member asked how they guaranteed that.\nThe trainer said, “We start before the city wakes up and finish before the roads do.”"],[["city"], "A passenger asked an auto driver to take a shortcut through the old market.\nThe driver agreed, then stopped to greet three shopkeepers.\nThe passenger said, “This shortcut seems to include a reunion.”"],[["city"], "The municipal garden introduced a self-service water tap.\nA visitor turned it on and waited for the sensor to respond.\nA gardener said, “It works best when you ask politely; the old one was very traditional.”"],[["city"], "A new co-working space advertised silence pods for focused work.\nA member entered one and heard a notification from the room next door.\nHe asked the receptionist if the pods came with noise-cancelling neighbours."],[["city"], "A commuter complained that the station escalator was out of service again.\nThe guard pointed to the staircase and said it was a healthy alternative.\nThe commuter replied, “I came for transport, not a surprise fitness assessment.”"],[["city"], "A local cinema introduced app-only ticket booking.\nAn uncle at the counter asked where to stand if his phone battery died.\nThe cashier pointed to the charging station and said, “The queue has moved to the socket.”"],[["city"], "The city council painted a fresh zebra crossing outside a school.\nA driver stopped and asked whether the stripes were still wet.\nThe traffic marshal said, “Only the paint; the patience test is permanent.”"],[["city"], "A florist delivered a bouquet to an office reception.\nThe receptionist asked who had sent it.\nThe florist checked the note and said, “Someone who knows this building has excellent lift music.”"],[["city"], "A roadside mechanic labelled his workshop “Quick Service.”\nA customer asked how quick the repairs usually were.\nThe mechanic said, “Quick enough to diagnose the problem before the tea gets cold.”"],[["city"], "A commuter bought a monthly pass and asked whether it covered unexpected delays.\nThe ticket clerk said the pass covered travel, not time.\nThe commuter replied, “Then please sell me the premium version of Monday morning.”"],[["city"], "A local newspaper asked residents what the city needed most.\nOne reader wrote, “More public benches and fewer meetings about public benches.”\nThe editor published it under the heading “A sitting matter.”"],[["city"], "A street cleaner found a wallet beside a bus stop and handed it to the police kiosk.\nThe officer asked how he knew it belonged to someone nearby.\n“He left his entire day's schedule inside,” the cleaner said."],[["city"], "A city tour guide pointed out a historic clock tower that had stopped years ago.\nA visitor asked why nobody repaired it.\nThe guide smiled: “It is the only landmark here that never complains about being late.”"],[["city"], "A commuter asked the bus driver if the next stop was the market.\nThe driver said, “If the traffic agrees.”\nThe commuter replied, “Please ask politely; my vegetables are waiting.”"],[["city"], "A city café advertised unlimited Wi-Fi.\nA customer asked for the password and received a long receipt.\n“Is it printed here?” he asked.\n“No,” said the waiter, “those are the terms and conditions.”"],[["city"], "A tourist asked a porter which train was fastest.\nThe porter pointed to the departure board.\n“Choose the one that leaves first,” he said, “the rest is railway philosophy.”"],[["city"], "A resident asked when the streetlight would be fixed.\nThe clerk requested the pole number.\n“It is the only one that goes dark every evening,” said the resident.\n“Excellent,” replied the clerk, “a well-lit description.”"],[["city"], "A cab passenger asked for the shortest route to the airport.\nThe driver opened the navigation app.\n“It knows many shortcuts,” he said, “but traffic has veto power.”"],[["city"], "A market vendor displayed a sign saying “Fixed prices”.\nA customer asked whether bargaining was allowed.\n“Of course,” said the vendor, “the price stays fixed while we bargain.”"],[["city"], "A commuter complained that the station escalator was broken.\nThe guard pointed to the stairs.\n“I paid for transport,” said the commuter, “not a surprise leg-day session.”"],[["city"], "A visitor asked how old the clock tower was.\nThe guide gave an estimate.\nThe visitor demanded the exact year.\n“The clock stopped,” said the guide, “but the history department is still running.”"],[["city"], "A neighbourhood shop began accepting digital payments.\nA customer asked whether cash was still welcome.\n“Absolutely,” said the owner, “our QR code is modern, but the drawer is sentimental.”"],[["city"], "A passenger asked an auto driver to avoid the crowded market.\nThe driver took a side lane and stopped at the same market entrance.\n“Different approach,” he explained, “same popular destination.”"],[["city"], "A park installed a board asking visitors to keep the grass clean.\nA man moved his picnic mat after reading it.\nThe gardener thanked him.\n“I don't want the grass to file a complaint,” he said."],[["city"], "A barber advertised a quick haircut.\nA customer asked how quick it was.\n“Ten minutes,” said the barber, “unless you want me to fix your last ten-minute haircut.”"],[["city"], "A train passenger asked if the train was delayed.\nThe conductor checked the board and confirmed it.\n“When will the delay end?” asked the passenger.\n“That part is still awaiting confirmation.”"],[["city"], "A food stall offered a “mild” option.\nA customer asked if it suited beginners.\nThe cook nodded and served it.\nThe customer reached for water: “I have graduated faster than expected.”"],[["city"], "A visitor asked the ferry operator to wait for one more passenger.\nThe operator checked the river.\n“We can wait for a person,” he said, “but not for the tide to change its mind.”"],[["city"], "A delivery rider called from the apartment gate.\nThe resident asked which gate he meant.\n“The one where security has requested more documents than the passport office,” replied the rider."],[["city"], "A library sent a reminder that a book was overdue.\nThe reader replied that he was still enjoying it.\nThe librarian wrote back, “Please enjoy it at the counter; the next reader is waiting.”"],[["city"], "A tourist asked for directions to the old market.\nThe shopkeeper gave two turns and a landmark.\n“Is there a simpler route?” asked the tourist.\n“Follow the smell of breakfast,” said the shopkeeper, “it never gets lost.”"],[["city"], "A commuter asked if the bus stopped near the hospital.\nThe conductor said it stopped outside.\n“How far outside?” asked the commuter.\n“Close enough to see it, far enough to finish your daily steps.”"],[["city"], "A café introduced QR-code menus.\nA customer scanned the code and found the menu, bill and feedback form.\n“Where is the coffee?” he asked.\n“That feature is still delivered by hand,” said the waiter."],[["city"], "A road crew placed a sign saying “Work in progress”.\nA resident asked when the work would finish.\nThe supervisor replied, “As soon as progress catches up with the sign.”"],[["city"], "A museum attendant said photography was allowed without flash.\nThe tourist put the phone away.\n“I will store the memory without cloud backup,” he said."],[["city"], "A parking attendant handed a driver a token.\nThe driver asked if it showed the parking slot.\n“No,” said the attendant, “it shows your place in the search for one.”"],[["city"], "A commuter asked how much time the new flyover saved.\n“Ten minutes on a good day,” said a colleague.\n“What about a bad day?”\n“Then we spend ten minutes explaining the good day.”"],[["city"], "A fruit seller advertised oranges as “sunshine in a bag”.\nA customer asked if they came with a weather guarantee.\n“Only if you promise not to keep them waiting in the fridge,” said the seller."],[["city"], "A mechanic labelled his shop “Quick Service”.\nA customer asked if the scooter would be ready before lunch.\nThe mechanic checked the parts shelf.\n“Certainly, if lunch is a flexible appointment.”"],[["city"], "A visitor asked why the old buildings were painted blue.\nThe guide explained the local tradition.\n“It makes the lanes beautiful,” said the visitor.\n“And helps lost tourists find the same photo spot,” added the guide."],[["city"], "A commuter asked if the pass covered unexpected delays.\nThe clerk said it covered travel, not time.\n“Then I need a separate pass for Monday mornings,” replied the commuter."],[["city"], "A resident complained that scooters blocked the footpath.\nThe shopkeeper said customers needed somewhere to stop.\n“A footpath is for feet,” said the resident, “the scooters can start their own walking group.”"],[["city"], "A guide pointed to a historic clock that had stopped years ago.\nA visitor asked why nobody repaired it.\n“It is the only landmark that never gets blamed for being late,” said the guide."],[["city"], "A Bengaluru startup founder booked a meeting room for a “quick sync.”\nThe calendar showed six attendees and a two-hour slot.\nThe receptionist asked whether it was still quick.\n“Of course,” he said, “we have only scheduled the discussion about scheduling the real discussion.”"],[["city"], "A visitor in Kochi asked an auto driver for the shortest route to the beach.\nThe driver pointed toward the ferry jetty.\n“Is that the road?” the visitor asked.\n“No,” said the driver, “that is the shortcut where the road takes a lunch break.”"],[["city"], "At a Pune bookshop, a student asked for a guide to time management.\nThe owner handed over a blank notebook.\n“Where are the tips?” asked the student.\n“First manage to open it every day,” the owner replied."],[["city"], "A tourist in Varanasi asked a boatman how old the riverfront was.\nThe boatman smiled and said the stories were older than the buildings.\nThe tourist asked for the exact date.\n“Madam,” he said, “even the river has stopped keeping receipts.”"],[["city"], "A Chennai commuter carried an umbrella on a cloudless morning.\nHis colleague asked why he was so cautious.\n“The forecast said scattered showers,” he replied.\n“I work in an office with a leaky ceiling; I prepare for local weather too.”"],[["city"], "A Surat textile trader advertised a “limited edition” fabric.\nA customer asked how limited it was.\n“Only three shops in this market have it,” he said.\nThe customer nodded: “So limited that I can compare prices before lunch.”"],[["city"], "A tourist in Amritsar asked where to find the city's best food.\nA local pointed toward a lane and said, “Follow the aroma.”\nThe tourist asked for a street name.\n“By the time you read the sign,” the local said, “your dinner will have found you.”"],[["city"], "In Indore, a man joined a queue after seeing everyone holding plates.\nHe asked what the line was for.\n“Poha,” someone said.\nHe stayed because, in that city, even breakfast had a stronger public following than his social media account."],[["city"], "A Hyderabad resident told a friend that the new flyover had saved ten minutes.\nThe friend asked what he did with the extra time.\n“Spent twelve minutes finding parking,” he said.\n“Urban planning is a team sport,” his friend replied."],[["city"], "A visitor in Shillong asked whether the clouds ever moved away.\nA shopkeeper looked up and said, “They do, but they leave their luggage here.”\nThe visitor bought a raincoat.\nThe shopkeeper added, “Good choice; the clouds are regular customers.”"],[["city"], "At a Delhi metro station, a tourist asked which side went to the museum.\nA commuter pointed to the map and explained the interchange.\nThe tourist thanked him and asked how long it would take.\n“Depends,” the commuter said, “on whether you admire every station announcement.”"],[["city"], "A Mysuru guide described the palace lights to a family.\nA child asked whether the palace looked the same in daylight.\n“Of course,” said the guide, “but at night it has remembered to dress up.”\nThe parents bought tickets for both visits."],[["city"], "A shopkeeper in Lucknow told a customer, “Please take your time.”\nThe customer spent twenty minutes choosing a pen.\nThe shopkeeper remained perfectly polite.\nAt last he said, “I meant take your time, not rent the whole afternoon.”"],[["city"], "A Nagpur resident told his cousin that the orange season had arrived.\nThe cousin asked whether every shop sold oranges.\n“Almost,” he said, “even the juice shop has started asking customers if they want a fruit with their straw.”"],[["city"], "A tourist in Jodhpur asked why the houses were painted blue.\nThe guide explained the history and local traditions.\nThe tourist asked if blue paint kept the rooms cool.\n“Not sure,” said the guide, “but it certainly makes lost visitors easier to spot.”"],[["city"], "In Ahmedabad, a friend invited another to a kite-flying session at sunrise.\nThe guest arrived at noon and asked if they were late.\nHis friend pointed to the sky, now full of kites.\n“You missed the beginning,” he said, “but the arguments over whose string is whose are still live.”"],[["city"], "A Kolkata tram passenger asked the conductor whether the tram was delayed.\nThe conductor checked the road and smiled.\n“Delayed compared with what?” he asked.\nThe passenger looked at the traffic and decided the tram was actually early for the city's pace."],[["city"], "A tourist in Udaipur asked a boat operator whether the lake was deep.\n“Deep enough for a boat,” came the reply.\nThe tourist asked if that was a scientific measurement.\n“No,” said the operator, “but it is the one that keeps everyone relaxed.”"],[["city"], "A Thiruvananthapuram resident told a visitor that the monsoon had arrived.\nThe visitor asked how he could tell.\nThe resident pointed to the balcony, where three umbrellas were drying.\n“One is for rain,” he said, “one is for the walk back, and one is for the forecast.”"],[["city"], "A Bhopal student asked a librarian for a quiet corner to study.\nThe librarian led him to a desk far from the entrance.\nThe student opened his laptop and joined a loud video call.\nThe librarian returned: “The corner is quiet; your Wi-Fi personality is not.”"],[["city"], "At a Guwahati tea stall, a visitor asked which tea was most popular.\nThe owner said, “The one people order while saying they are in a hurry.”\nThe visitor ordered it and sat down.\nFive minutes later, he was asking for the local news too."],[["city"], "A resident of Noida told a friend his new apartment was close to everything.\nThe friend asked how close the grocery shop was.\n“Two minutes by map,” he said.\n“And in real life?” asked the friend. “That depends on the lift's career goals.”"],[["city"], "A tourist in Madurai asked a flower seller how long the garland would stay fresh.\nThe seller replied that it would last through the day's celebrations.\nThe tourist asked for a guarantee.\n“Sir,” she said, “I can promise the flowers; the weather has its own terms and conditions.”"],[["city"], "A visitor in Panaji asked a fisherman whether the sea was calm.\nHe looked at the water and said it was calm enough for the morning.\nThe visitor asked about the afternoon.\n“Ask the sea after lunch,” the fisherman said, “it does not share its calendar.”"],[["city"], "A resident of Kanpur complained that the local market was too crowded.\nHis friend asked why he still shopped there.\n“Because the prices are good,” he replied.\n“And the crowd?” “That is the market's free shoulder massage.”"],[["city"], "A tourist in Dharamshala asked a café owner for a table with a mountain view.\nThe owner pointed to a window seat.\nThe tourist asked whether clouds might block the view.\n“Only temporarily,” said the owner. “Here, even the mountains believe in privacy.”"],[["city"], "A Jaipur student asked a shopkeeper for a notebook with a hard cover.\nThe shopkeeper showed three options and explained the paper quality.\nThe student chose the cheapest one.\n“Good,” said the shopkeeper, “your budget has passed its entrance exam.”"],[["city"], "A Mumbai visitor asked a local how long the sea link drive would take.\nThe local said it depended on the traffic at either end.\nThe visitor asked if the bridge itself was fast.\n“Very,” said the local, “it is the approaches that enjoy sightseeing.”"],[["city"], "A resident of Patna told his friend that the new café had “authentic quiet.”\nThe friend asked what that meant.\n“No loud music, no television, no announcements,” he said.\n“Just the grinder,” the friend guessed. “Exactly; it has a solo career.”"],[["city"], "A tourist in Gangtok asked a driver if the road ahead was steep.\nThe driver nodded and advised taking it slowly.\nThe tourist asked whether the view was worth it.\nThe driver smiled: “You will stop asking about the road once the clouds open the curtains.”"]]);

/* en-IN expansion batch 02: 100 Culture Contrasts + 100 Marriage jokes. */
window.JESTBOX_JOKES["en-IN"].push(...[[["culture-contrasts"],"A visiting colleague removed their shoes before entering the office pantry.\nThe host explained that only the meeting room had a shoe policy.\nThe colleague said the pantry had earned more respect than the boardroom."],[["culture-contrasts"],"At a festival lunch, one guest asked whether the food was spicy.\nThe host said “medium”, while three relatives offered three different definitions.\nThe guest wisely began with a small spoon and a large glass of water."],[["culture-contrasts"],"Two friends debated whether arriving ten minutes late counted as punctual.\nOne checked the calendar invitation; the other checked the family custom.\nThey agreed to meet at a time that could survive both interpretations."],[["culture-contrasts"],"A colleague brought homemade snacks to a team celebration.\nEveryone asked for the recipe, then asked whether it could be made without the main ingredient.\nThe cook suggested they begin by appreciating the original version."],[["culture-contrasts"],"At a wedding, the band played a familiar tune in an unfamiliar rhythm.\nThe grandparents recognised the melody, while the children recognised the dance challenge.\nThree generations agreed the song had excellent cross-platform compatibility."],[["culture-contrasts"],"A guest asked whether it was customary to bring a small gift.\nThe host said the visit itself was enough.\nThe guest arrived with sweets anyway, because customs also travel with luggage."],[["culture-contrasts"],"The office arranged a potluck and asked everyone to label their dishes.\nOne label listed ingredients, another listed allergens, and a third simply said “trust me”.\nThe organiser placed that dish beside the emergency biscuits."],[["culture-contrasts"],"A friend translated a proverb literally for an international visitor.\nThe visitor understood every word and none of the advice.\nThey agreed the meaning needed its own passport."],[["culture-contrasts"],"At a family gathering, two people disagreed about the correct way to greet elders.\nOne preferred a handshake, the other a respectful bow.\nThe elder settled it by asking who had brought the sweets."],[["culture-contrasts"],"A team tried to choose one language for a group presentation.\nThey chose simple English, then added local examples so nobody felt left out.\nThe slides were concise; the discussion became beautifully multilingual."],[["culture-contrasts"],"At a family potluck, the Gujarati side brought dhokla and the Punjabi side brought chole.\nThe host asked everyone to leave room for dessert; both sides interpreted that as a challenge.\nThe dessert table had to apply for an extension."],[["culture-contrasts"],"An office team planned a “quick lunch” with colleagues from four states.\nThe menu discussion took longer than the meeting they had skipped.\nThe minutes recorded one unanimous decision: order extra."],[["culture-contrasts"],"At a multilingual wedding, the DJ announced the next song in three languages.\nEvery group cheered at a different sentence and started dancing at once.\nThe dance floor became the only place where everyone understood the agenda."],[["culture-contrasts"],"A guest said they preferred mild food at a regional dinner.\nThe host served a mild version and placed the original chutney nearby for “optional research.”\nThe guest's water glass became the evening's most popular companion."],[["culture-contrasts"],"Two friends debated whether tea or coffee was the better afternoon break.\nA third friend ordered both and asked them to settle the issue over snacks.\nThe debate ended when the snacks ran out."],[["culture-contrasts"],"At a shared office lunch, one colleague brought thepla and another brought parathas.\nThey compared recipes and discovered both families had a secret ingredient: extra ghee.\nThe nutrition app quietly left the conversation."],[["culture-contrasts"],"Friends from different regions debated the correct way to eat poha.\nOne added sev, another added lemon, and a third asked for curd.\nThe plate became a cultural exchange programme with no neutral observer."],[["culture-contrasts"],"At a festival gathering, guests greeted each other in several languages.\nThe host replied in all of them, then forgot where the snacks were kept.\nEveryone understood the directions once the aroma arrived."],[["culture-contrasts"],"A colleague called a meal “not too spicy” and confidently took the first bite.\nThe next minute involved water, yoghurt, and a detailed review of the chilli level.\nThe cook said the dish had passed its regional welcome test."],[["culture-contrasts"],"Two families planned a picnic and argued about the ideal start time.\nOne group meant sunrise; the other meant after a leisurely breakfast.\nThey settled on a time that required both an alarm and a second cup of tea."],[["culture-contrasts"], "A family asked the youngest cousin to explain the new video-call app.\nHe demonstrated the mute button, then watched six elders keep talking to a muted screen.\nThe family declared the feature excellent for uninterrupted speeches."],[["culture-contrasts"], "At a potluck, one guest brought a handwritten recipe card.\nAnother guest scanned it, translated it and sent it to the group chat.\nThe cook asked for the original back; it had become a family-owned digital asset."],[["culture-contrasts"], "My neighbour says their home is shoes-off.\nMy relatives say shoes-off, slippers-on, and please take these snacks too.\nThe doorway has become a complete hospitality transition zone."],[["culture-contrasts"], "A friend asked whether our family celebrates birthdays quietly.\nI said yes, until someone brings out the cake and three people start giving speeches.\nThe candles are usually extinguished by the time the first toast ends."],[["culture-contrasts"], "One cousin insists every family photo needs a countdown.\nAnother believes the best picture happens when nobody is ready.\nOur album now has 40 posed smiles and one masterpiece of everyone laughing."],[["culture-contrasts"], "My colleague calls it a packed lunch.\nMy grandmother calls it food from home and asks why I bought a container.\nThe container has a name now and attends every office meeting."],[["culture-contrasts"], "At a family function, the seating chart listed everyone's name.\nThe relatives rearranged the chairs according to who had travelled furthest.\nThe organiser called it a dynamic seating model with strong community input."],[["culture-contrasts"], "My friend says their family shares one dessert equally.\nAt ours, everyone says \"just a taste\" and brings a spoon the size of a serving bowl.\nThe dessert disappears, but the debate about fairness lasts until tea."],[["culture-contrasts"], "A guest asked if they should help clear the table.\nThe host said no, then handed them a container for leftovers.\nThey left as a guest and returned home as the household's logistics partner."],[["culture-contrasts"], "My parents keep the TV remote in a fixed place.\nMy siblings keep moving it to test whether the family still communicates.\nWe found it under a cushion and called the search a team-building exercise."],[["culture-contrasts"], "At a multilingual dinner, everyone knew the word for \"more\".\nNobody knew the word for \"I am full\" in a way the aunties would accept.\nThe translation team eventually surrendered to another serving."],[["culture-contrasts"], "My friend labels every storage box by season.\nMy family labels boxes \"important\", \"very important\" and \"do not open\".\nThe one marked \"do not open\" contains three other boxes with the same label."],[["culture-contrasts"], "One household plans a holiday with a spreadsheet.\nAnother waits for a relative to say, \"Let's see where the road takes us.\"\nBoth arrived at the same destination, but only one brought printed backups."],[["culture-contrasts"], "At a wedding, the photographer asked everyone to look natural.\nThe family immediately stood in two straight rows and stopped blinking.\nThe photographer said, \"Perfect, now pretend this is not a formal inspection.\""],[["culture-contrasts"], "My aunt asks whether I want tea before asking my name.\nMy friend's host asks about dietary preferences before offering a chair.\nBoth make guests feel welcome; one simply starts the onboarding earlier."],[["culture-contrasts"], "A colleague explained that their family uses three calendars.\nOne tracks public holidays, one tracks religious occasions and one tracks birthdays.\nThe shared calendar is mostly reminders to check the other calendars."],[["culture-contrasts"], "My cousin says a family gathering is a chance to catch up.\nMy uncle says it is a chance to ask why I have not called.\nI now arrive with stories, snacks and a fully charged phone."],[["culture-contrasts"], "At a shared meal, one guest asked for a fork and another offered a spoon.\nThe host brought both, plus a serving of the dish that required neither.\nThe table reached consensus without a formal vote."],[["culture-contrasts"], "My friend says their family wraps gifts neatly.\nMy family saves the wrapping paper, the ribbon and the box for the next occasion.\nThe gift is temporary; the packaging has a long-term career."],[["culture-contrasts"], "At the end of a festival, everyone offered to help clean up.\nThe host said, \"No need,\" while handing out containers and assigning the leftovers.\nThe clean-up was complete before anyone admitted it had started."],[["culture-contrasts"], "Festival season at the apartment gate.\nA visitor asked why every family had a different welcome ritual.\nThe guard said, “Because even the lift gets invited to celebrations here.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "A new colleague asked whether lunch breaks were flexible.\nThe team said yes, then debated whose regional food smelled best.\nThe meeting ended only when someone opened the tiffin."],[["culture-contrasts"], "At a family gathering, an aunt asked the newcomer to try one sweet.\nThe newcomer politely chose the smallest piece.\nThe aunt returned with a plate and called it a sampling exercise."],[["culture-contrasts"], "A tourist asked why the street had two names.\nA resident explained the official name and the name everyone actually used.\nThe tourist saved both, then asked which one the taxi understood."],[["culture-contrasts"], "During a wedding, the photographer requested everyone look at the camera.\nThree relatives looked at their phones to check the camera angle.\nThe photographer declared the family digitally well aligned."],[["culture-contrasts"], "A guest asked whether the meal was spicy.\nThe host said, “Only if your ancestors came from somewhere else.”\nThe guest reached for water and received a family history lesson."],[["culture-contrasts"], "An office team planned a festival potluck.\nOne person labelled a dish “mild” and another labelled it “mild for my hometown”.\nHR added a spice-risk disclaimer to the invite."],[["culture-contrasts"], "A visitor asked why people removed footwear before entering.\nThe host explained the custom and pointed to the shoe rack.\nThe visitor said, “Good, my shoes needed a cultural break too.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "At a neighbourhood celebration, the music changed every few minutes.\nOne uncle danced to every language without knowing the lyrics.\nHe said rhythm was the only translation he needed."],[["culture-contrasts"], "A newcomer asked how to greet elders at a family function.\nThe cousin demonstrated a respectful greeting and a dozen name-based variations.\nThe newcomer practised until even the elders approved the rehearsal."],[["culture-contrasts"], "A friend moved from one state to another and asked about local breakfast.\nThe host listed six dishes and three acceptable chutneys.\nThe friend realised breakfast had become a regional entrance exam."],[["culture-contrasts"], "At a community event, two volunteers argued over the correct queue.\nOne followed the sign; the other followed the crowd.\nThe organiser created a third queue for people asking which queue was correct."],[["culture-contrasts"], "A visitor asked why the family kept offering more food.\nThe host said, “We believe hunger can return during conversation.”\nThe visitor accepted another serving to avoid a lengthy research discussion."],[["culture-contrasts"], "An international guest asked whether a festival date changed every year.\nThe host opened three calendars and called a relative for confirmation.\nThe guest said, “I see; the calendar has a consultation process.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "At a railway platform, a traveller asked which side the train would arrive on.\nA local pointed to the display, then to the crowd, then to the tea stall.\n“Watch all three,” the local said, “one of them is always right.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "A colleague brought homemade regional snacks to work.\nEveryone asked for the recipe, but nobody asked for the measurements.\nThe cook said, “The secret ingredient is knowing when to stop explaining.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "At a family video call, everyone spoke at once.\nThe youngest muted the call to restore order.\nGrandfather said, “Excellent, now we can hear the silence in every language.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "A visitor asked why the farewell at the door took so long.\nThe host said the goodbye included travel advice, leftovers and three safety reminders.\nThe visitor reached the car with enough food for the journey and the next one."],[["culture-contrasts"], "Two friends compared wedding customs from their regions.\nEach insisted their ceremony had the most complicated schedule.\nThe planner quietly introduced them to the spreadsheet."],[["culture-contrasts"], "A shopkeeper switched languages when a customer looked confused.\nThe customer replied in a third language and asked for a discount.\nThe shopkeeper said, “Now we are truly communicating.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "At a cultural programme, the announcer mispronounced a place name.\nThe audience corrected it in four accents at once.\nThe announcer thanked them and called it live pronunciation training."],[["culture-contrasts"], "A guest asked whether they should bring a gift to dinner.\nThe host said, “Just bring yourself.”\nThe guest arrived with dessert anyway, because local customs have footnotes."],[["culture-contrasts"], "At a festival market, a visitor asked why bargaining was expected.\nThe seller said the first price was an introduction, not a conclusion.\nThe visitor asked for the syllabus before negotiating."],[["culture-contrasts"], "A family tried to take one group photograph.\nEvery generation suggested a different pose and camera setting.\nThe final picture captured the photographer asking for patience."],[["culture-contrasts"], "An exchange student asked why the same dish tasted different in every home.\nThe host said every household had its own version of the recipe.\nThe student wrote down “ingredient: family confidence”."],[["culture-contrasts"], "At a local bus stop, a newcomer asked whether the bus was crowded.\nA regular passenger said, “Not yet; there is still room for optimism.”\nThe bus arrived and optimism boarded first."],[["culture-contrasts"], "A guest complimented the host's traditional outfit.\nThe host explained its fabric, region and occasion in impressive detail.\nThe guest said, “I asked about the outfit and got a guided museum tour.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "During a festival cleanup, neighbours debated where decorations belonged.\nOne person measured the wall while another consulted the elders.\nThe children solved it by putting the decorations where the snacks were."],[["culture-contrasts"], "A visitor asked how long a family celebration would last.\nThe host checked the clock and said, “The formal part ends at eight.”\nThe visitor asked about the informal part; the host laughed, “We don't publish that timetable.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "At a multicultural office lunch, everyone brought a dish from home.\nThe team ran out of plates before running out of food.\nThe manager called it the most successful cross-functional collaboration of the quarter."],[["culture-contrasts"], "An exchange student asked why the class timetable had a separate assembly slot.\nA local explained the announcements, prayers and last-minute notices.\nThe student said, “So the school has a daily all-hands meeting.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "A teacher asked the class to explain a regional proverb.\nOne student gave the literal translation; another gave the family version.\nThe teacher marked both correct and added “context required”."],[["culture-contrasts"], "At a school cultural day, the organiser asked everyone to arrive in costume.\nOne student arrived dressed as a calendar.\nHe said, “I represent every regional holiday we are still negotiating.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "A parent asked why the school WhatsApp group was so active.\nThe teacher said it was mostly reminders.\nThe parent replied, “I have received three reminders about the reminder.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "A visiting professor asked how students prepared for exams.\nThe class described notes, group study and past papers.\nOne student added, “And a backup plan for the printer.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "Two classmates compared lunch boxes from different states.\nThey swapped food and argued about whose pickle was strongest.\nThe teacher called it a practical lesson in comparative chemistry."],[["culture-contrasts"], "A student submitted an assignment with a beautifully decorated cover.\nThe teacher praised the artwork and asked about the research.\nThe student said, “The cover is the executive summary.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "At a college fest, the emcee announced a multilingual quiz.\nThe first question was translated into four languages.\nThe audience answered in a fifth and asked for bonus marks."],[["culture-contrasts"], "A newcomer asked why every family seemed to know the school principal.\nThe neighbour said, “Because school matters are community matters.”\nThe newcomer asked whether the principal had a separate community manager."],[["culture-contrasts"], "A student asked whether attendance was taken during online class.\nThe teacher said yes, through the chat window.\nThe student typed “present” and then asked if the internet could sign too."],[["culture-contrasts"], "At the neighbourhood's international food fair, the organiser labelled every dish with its region.\nA visitor asked where the “Indian food” stall was.\nThe volunteer pointed to the entire ground and said, “We tried to give it one table, but the map ran out of space.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "A colleague from abroad asked why a family function had three different start times.\nThe host explained the invitation time, the auspicious time and the time guests actually arrive.\nThe colleague nodded: “So your event has a schedule and a live version.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "The exchange student thought the building's lift had stopped because everyone was waiting silently.\nA resident explained that the power had gone and the generator was being discussed in the residents' group.\n“Is there a backup?” asked the student.\n“Yes,” said the resident, “a very active discussion about the backup.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "At a language club, two friends translated the same greeting into English.\nOne chose the formal version; the other used the phrase their grandmother would say.\nThe tutor accepted both and wrote, “Translation is easy; explaining the relationship takes the whole class.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "A visiting researcher asked why the wedding invitation listed so many relatives by title.\nThe family explained that each title carried a different responsibility.\nThe researcher said, “In my country we use a spreadsheet.”\nThe uncle replied, “We do too, but ours has emotions in every column.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "A tourist asked whether the local market had fixed prices.\nThe shopkeeper said the price was fixed, but the conversation was flexible.\nThe tourist paid and smiled: “I came for a souvenir and got a negotiation workshop.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "The office exchange programme paired two employees to compare lunch habits.\nOne packed a measured salad; the other opened a steel tiffin with four compartments.\nBy noon, the salad had a new colleague and the tiffin had acquired a fan club."],[["culture-contrasts"], "A visitor asked why the festival calendar showed several New Years.\nThe guide explained that communities marked the season in different ways.\nThe visitor said, “That sounds complicated.”\nThe guide replied, “Only if you insist on celebrating just one.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "At a cultural orientation, the trainer asked what “just five minutes” meant locally.\nThe group offered answers ranging from a quick errand to an entire family visit.\nThe trainer added a new glossary entry: “Duration depends on who has arrived.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "A student compared two regional versions of the same folk tale.\nThe first ended with a clever merchant; the second ended with a clever grandmother.\nThe teacher asked which was authentic.\nThe student said, “Both. The lesson changes when the storyteller changes.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "A guest asked why everyone removed footwear before entering the house.\nThe host explained the custom and offered a place for the shoes.\nThe guest asked whether it was compulsory.\nThe host smiled: “No, but the floor has a very strong preference.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "The new employee asked why the team celebrated a project launch with sweets.\nA colleague explained that sharing something sweet was a way to mark good news.\nThe employee brought cupcakes for the next milestone.\nThe team asked whether the next release could be scheduled before lunch."],[["culture-contrasts"], "A visitor heard three languages during one bus ride and asked which one was official.\nThe conductor answered in one, the passenger replied in another, and the driver used a third.\nThe visitor said, “How do you all understand each other?”\nThe conductor pointed at the destination board: “We agree on where the bus is going.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "A family hosted guests from another state and asked about their preferred breakfast.\nThe guests requested something light.\nThe kitchen served fruit, poha, idli and enough chutneys to require a seating plan.\nThe host said, “We kept it simple; the debate is optional.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "The museum guide explained how one craft used different motifs in neighbouring districts.\nA visitor asked which pattern was the original.\nThe guide said, “The original is the one your grandmother recognises.”\nThe visitor called home to settle the matter."],[["culture-contrasts"], "At a workplace potluck, everyone brought a dish from home.\nOne colleague labelled theirs “mild” to be considerate.\nThe first bite made the team reach for water.\nThe colleague clarified, “Mild by my family's standards; I should have added a footnote.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "A student asked why a local greeting changed depending on the elder's age.\nThe teacher explained that language can carry respect as well as information.\nThe student practised three versions.\nThe teacher said, “Good. Now learn which one your aunt expects.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "A visitor wondered why the community hall had separate noticeboards for different festivals.\nThe caretaker explained that each group maintained its own announcements.\nThe visitor suggested one shared board.\nThe caretaker replied, “We tried; the board needed its own festival.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "The exchange student asked whether the town's old recipes were written down.\nA neighbour said most were taught by watching and tasting.\nThe student asked for exact measurements.\nThe neighbour handed over a spoon and said, “First learn what ‘a little’ looks like in this kitchen.”"],[["culture-contrasts"], "At the end of a regional arts workshop, the instructor asked what everyone had learned.\nOne participant said the same instrument sounded different in every tradition.\nAnother added that the rhythm changed with the story.\nThe instructor smiled: “Excellent. You have discovered why the programme needs a longer slot.”"],[["marriage"], "A couple booked a cooking class to learn one signature dish.\nThey returned with matching aprons and a disagreement about what “a pinch” means.\nThe instructor called it a successful lesson in shared decision-making."],[["marriage"], "At a family wedding, the couple planned a quiet exit after the ceremony.\nTheir relatives formed a farewell corridor with snacks and travel advice.\nThe getaway car left with enough food for a week."],[["marriage"], "One spouse labelled the pantry shelves to make mornings easier.\nThe other added labels explaining which labels were suggestions.\nTheir household policy document is now longer than the grocery list."],[["marriage"], "The couple adopted a plant and agreed to care for it together.\nEach watered it on alternate days, so the plant received twice the recommended amount.\nTheir first parenting lesson came from a very soggy pot."],[["marriage"], "During a power cut, one partner lit candles while the other searched for the inverter.\nThey spent the evening talking instead of watching television.\nThe next day they installed a backup plan for more conversations."],[["marriage"], "A husband offered to plan the family holiday and asked for complete freedom.\nHis wife agreed, provided he checked school dates, train tickets and everyone's leave.\nHe discovered freedom came with a shared spreadsheet."],[["marriage"], "The couple tried to assemble a wardrobe without calling the carpenter.\nAfter three hours, they had one door, four spare screws and new respect for professionals.\nThe wardrobe was finished the following weekend by an expert."],[["marriage"], "At their anniversary, friends asked how they kept romance alive.\nOne said, “We still surprise each other.”\nThe other added, “Mostly by finding the electricity bill before the due date.”"],[["marriage"], "One partner bought a fitness band for the other as a gift.\nThe recipient wore it proudly until it began reminding them to move during a movie.\nThey negotiated a truce: steps count, but cliff-hangers do not."],[["marriage"], "The couple agreed to host a small dinner for four guests.\nTheir relatives interpreted “small” as a seating arrangement, not a headcount.\nThe dining table became a logistics project with dessert as the contingency plan."],[["marriage"], "A spouse asked for honest feedback on a new haircut.\nThe other paused, remembered the wedding vows and chose a diplomatic adjective.\nThe haircut was called “bold”; the silence was called “supportive”."],[["marriage"], "On moving day, one partner packed kitchen items while the other packed books.\nBoth labelled every box “essentials”.\nThe movers asked whether the new home had a library or a restaurant."],[["marriage"], "The couple set a rule to discuss big purchases together.\nOne arrived with a new mixer and called it a small appliance.\nThe other brought home a sofa and called it a seating accessory."],[["marriage"], "At a wedding rehearsal, the planner asked the couple to practise walking slowly.\nThey kept speeding up whenever they saw the buffet.\nThe planner added “avoid eye contact with snacks” to the rehearsal notes."],[["marriage"], "One spouse made a playlist for a long drive.\nThe other added navigation instructions between every two songs.\nThey arrived on time, musically informed and mildly over-briefed."],[["marriage"], "The couple decided to declutter their home together.\nEvery object had a story, a memory or a possible future use.\nBy sunset, they had organised the memories and kept all the objects."],[["marriage"], "A partner asked, “What should we have for dinner?”\nThe other suggested five options, each rejected for a different reason.\nThey finally ordered the first suggestion and called it consensus."],[["marriage"], "At a family function, one spouse introduced the other to a distant relative.\nThe relative asked how they were related and received a full family tree.\nDessert arrived before the explanation reached the cousin branch."],[["marriage"], "The couple bought matching luggage for a trip.\nAt the airport, both picked up the wrong suitcase because the labels were identical.\nThey now believe personalisation is a travel essential."],[["marriage"], "One partner promised to fix the dripping tap over the weekend.\nThe other placed a bucket underneath and named it the household water feature.\nThe plumber arrived Monday to find the bucket had gained a fan club."],[["marriage"], "They decided to save money by preparing coffee at home.\nThe first week went well until they bought a grinder, frother and premium beans.\nTheir accountant called it a café acquisition."],[["marriage"], "At a parent-teacher meeting, the couple agreed to let one person speak.\nBoth began with, “Just one small point.”\nThe teacher scheduled a follow-up meeting and brought extra tea."],[["marriage"], "The newlyweds created a shared photo album.\nOne uploaded scenic pictures; the other uploaded receipts and booking confirmations.\nThe album became the most accurate record of their holiday."],[["marriage"], "A spouse asked for a weekend with no plans.\nThe other interpreted this as an opportunity to schedule rest, naps and optional relaxation.\nThey spent Sunday recovering from the planning."],[["marriage"], "The couple tried a board game after dinner.\nThey disagreed about one rule and consulted the instruction booklet.\nThe game ended when they both declared the booklet the winner."],[["marriage"], "One partner volunteered to water the balcony garden during a trip.\nThe other left a chart with plant names, quantities and timings.\nThe neighbour said the plants had better travel documentation than most tourists."],[["marriage"], "At the supermarket, the couple split up to finish shopping faster.\nThey both returned with rice, detergent and the same brand of biscuits.\nThe only missing item was the one written at the top of the list."],[["marriage"], "The couple decided to learn a new language together.\nOne practised vocabulary while the other practised pronunciation.\nTheir first fluent sentence was, “Please correct me gently.”"],[["marriage"], "One spouse surprised the other with a home-cooked meal.\nThe table was set beautifully, but the recipe had been doubled by mistake.\nThey invited the neighbours and called it an anniversary extension."],[["marriage"], "At a family gathering, the couple were asked who made the final decisions at home.\nThey answered together, “Whoever has checked the facts.”\nThe family asked for the same system at the next wedding committee meeting."],[["marriage"], "The couple installed a smart speaker to simplify household routines.\nIt kept misunderstanding their requests and playing workout music.\nThey decided the device had become the most energetic member of the family."],[["marriage"], "One partner suggested a surprise road trip.\nThe other asked whether the car was serviced, the route checked and snacks packed.\nThe surprise was that the checklist was already printed."],[["marriage"], "At their anniversary, the couple exchanged handwritten notes.\nOne wrote a poem; the other wrote favourite shared memories.\nBoth agreed the best line promised to keep choosing each other."],[["marriage"], "The couple agreed to split the bill at a restaurant.\nOne calculated the food, the other calculated taxes and tip.\nThe waiter returned with a calculator and asked if they were celebrating an audit."],[["marriage"], "One spouse asked the other to take a candid photograph.\nThe photographer adjusted the light, moved a chair and requested three retakes.\nThe subject said, “That was a lovely candid production.”"],[["marriage"], "The couple agreed to host a quiet wedding reception.\nTheir families each invited only a few close relatives.\nThe venue manager asked whether the other 240 guests were the catering team."],[["marriage"], "A newly married pair made a shared household budget.\nOne entered groceries; the other entered festival shopping.\nThe spreadsheet added a new column called 'unexpected relatives'."],[["marriage"], "The bride and groom chose a playlist together.\nThey approved every song except the one both secretly loved.\nThe DJ played it anyway, and both blamed the other's request."],[["marriage"], "A couple planned their first holiday after the wedding.\nOne packed light; the other packed medicines, chargers and documents.\nThe suitcase looked ready to apply for its own passport."],[["marriage"], "The couple tried assembling a wardrobe without help.\nThey followed the diagram carefully but still had one spare panel.\nThe instruction sheet called it 'future expansion'."],[["marriage"], "At dinner, one spouse asked for an honest opinion on a new recipe.\nThe other paused, took another bite and asked for the recipe link.\nThe cook accepted that as a five-star review."],[["marriage"], "The couple agreed to take turns choosing a weekend activity.\nOne chose a museum; the other chose a long walk.\nThey spent the afternoon debating which gift shop had better snacks."],[["marriage"], "A spouse bought matching mugs for their anniversary.\nThe other asked why both mugs had different names.\nThe answer was, 'So we can identify the one you keep borrowing'."],[["marriage"], "The couple made a rule to avoid phones during dinner.\nTheir smart watch kept displaying notifications.\nThey put it in a bowl and called the bowl the family IT department."],[["marriage"], "At a wedding, the couple asked guests to write one piece of advice.\nOne card said, 'Always communicate clearly.'\nThe next card said, 'Especially about who is bringing the return gifts'."],[["marriage"], "The newlyweds decided to divide household chores fairly.\nOne took cooking; the other took dishes.\nThey both tried to negotiate ownership of the dishwasher."],[["marriage"], "A couple went furniture shopping with exact measurements.\nThe salesperson asked whether they had measured the doorway too.\nThey went home with a measuring tape and a new respect for geometry."],[["marriage"], "One spouse surprised the other with breakfast in bed.\nThe tray was perfect, but the toast was still in the toaster.\nThey called it an interactive breakfast experience."],[["marriage"], "The couple made a shared calendar for family events.\nEvery relative added a birthday and a preferred reminder.\nThe calendar requested a day off."],[["marriage"], "A spouse suggested a spontaneous dinner outing.\nThe other asked whether spontaneous meant booked, budgeted or nearby.\nThey chose a restaurant and labelled the plan 'controlled spontaneity'."],[["marriage"], "At a family function, the couple tried to leave quietly.\nAn aunt spotted them near the gate and began a fresh conversation.\nTheir goodbye required a second round of tea."],[["marriage"], "The couple decided to learn dancing before a wedding.\nThey practised the steps in the living room.\nThe neighbour asked whether the furniture was part of the choreography."],[["marriage"], "One partner labelled containers in the kitchen.\nThe other added dates and reheating instructions.\nThe leftovers now had a better records policy than the office."],[["marriage"], "A couple compared their first-year wedding photographs.\nThey noticed the same uncle appeared in every group picture.\nHe said he was simply supporting the event's visual continuity."],[["marriage"], "The newlyweds planned a housewarming with a guest list.\nThey counted chairs, plates and parking spaces.\nThe final list included one extra chair for whoever arrived with a surprise guest."],[["marriage"], "One spouse asked for a small birthday celebration.\nThe family brought a cake, flowers and a microphone.\nThe birthday person learned that 'small' was not a legally binding term."],[["marriage"], "The couple tried to choose curtains together.\nOne preferred a calm neutral shade; the other wanted bright patterns.\nThe shopkeeper suggested they start with two separate windows."],[["marriage"], "A spouse promised to fix a dripping tap on Sunday.\nSunday arrived with a toolbox and a tutorial video.\nBy evening, the tap worked and the bathroom had a new vocabulary."],[["marriage"], "The couple ordered groceries online for the week.\nBoth independently added coriander to the cart.\nThe delivery person asked whether they were opening a restaurant."],[["marriage"], "At a reception, the couple cut the cake together.\nThe knife stopped halfway through the icing.\nA cousin announced that even the cake wanted a joint decision."],[["marriage"], "The couple tried to keep a plant alive after moving house.\nThey created a watering schedule and assigned a backup caretaker.\nThe plant thrived once everyone stopped holding meetings around it."],[["marriage"], "One partner asked for directions during a road trip.\nThe other said the map was clear and the turn was obvious.\nThey passed the turn while agreeing that the map was technically correct."],[["marriage"], "A couple planned a no-spend weekend.\nThey visited a public garden and carried homemade snacks.\nThe only expense was buying a bigger container for the snacks."],[["marriage"], "The family asked the newlyweds who would manage the finances.\nThey said they would review every expense together.\nThe uncle replied, 'Excellent, please review the wedding bill first'."],[["marriage"], "One spouse wanted to keep old greeting cards.\nThe other suggested scanning them to save space.\nThey compromised by keeping the funniest cards in a very small box."],[["marriage"], "The couple booked a home repair visit for the morning.\nThe technician arrived exactly on time.\nThe relatives who had promised to help arrived after the work was finished."],[["marriage"], "At a family dinner, someone asked for the secret to a happy marriage.\nThe couple answered, 'Listen carefully and share the remote.'\nThe television was immediately switched off for a serious discussion."],[["marriage"], "The couple decided to cook a new dish every month.\nTheir first attempt needed three pans and a second recipe search.\nThey named it 'experimental cuisine with strong teamwork'."],[["marriage"], "One partner bought a surprise gift and hid it carefully.\nThe other found it while looking for the spare batteries.\nThe surprise survived because neither remembered what the gift was."],[["marriage"], "A couple made a photo book of their first year together.\nThey included trips, meals and ordinary Sunday mornings.\nThe printer suggested a second volume titled 'Where did the weekend go?'."],[["marriage"], "The newlyweds installed a doorbell camera.\nIt recorded every delivery and every neighbour's greeting.\nThe couple discovered their most frequent visitor was the courier."],[["marriage"], "A spouse asked whether the new sofa looked good in the room.\nThe other measured the space and checked the walking path.\nThe answer was, 'Yes, and we can still reach the kitchen'."],[["marriage"], "The couple agreed to alternate visits between both families.\nThey created a fair travel schedule.\nThe relatives responded by planning a joint lunch halfway between the houses."],[["marriage"], "At the wedding anniversary, one spouse asked what had changed most.\nThe other said, 'We now know which drawer contains every charger.'\nThey agreed that was a milestone worth celebrating."],[["marriage"], "The couple tried a shared fitness challenge.\nOne tracked steps while the other tracked water intake.\nTheir most successful day was the walk to refill the water bottles."],[["marriage"], "The couple made a list of wedding gifts to thank each guest.\nOne gift had no card, no name and an unusually large bow.\nThe family opened a detective group chat before opening the box."],[["marriage"], "The newlyweds received matching luggage.\nOne suitcase had a label saying “his”; the other said “shared”.\nThey knew the family had already settled the packing policy."],[["marriage"], "The couple planned a low-key anniversary.\nTheir relatives booked a hall, ordered a band and invited the neighbourhood.\nThe couple celebrated quietly by hiding in the kitchen."],[["marriage"], "The planner asked the couple to approve the seating chart.\nThey moved one chair to avoid an old family disagreement.\nThe chart immediately needed a version-control system."],[["marriage"], "The couple tried to choose a wedding hashtag.\nEvery suggestion was already taken by another couple.\nThey finally chose one nobody could spell, ensuring privacy."],[["marriage"], "The bride requested a simple floral arrangement.\nThe decorator arrived with a portfolio and a drone.\nThe flowers were simple; the delivery had a launch sequence."],[["marriage"], "The groom promised to keep his wedding speech short.\nHe wrote three lines and practised them all week.\nThe family requested an encore before he finished the first line."],[["marriage"], "At the reception, the couple wanted to greet every guest.\nOne uncle kept introducing them to people they had just greeted.\nThey completed the evening with a very polite loop."],[["marriage"], "The couple asked guests not to bring boxed gifts.\nOne relative arrived with a large plant in a larger pot.\nThe gift complied with the rule and challenged the luggage allowance."],[["marriage"], "The newlyweds tried to take a day off after the wedding.\nTheir phones kept receiving photographs from five different relatives.\nThey renamed the day “post-production review”."],[["marriage"], "A couple compared honeymoon hotel options.\nOne prioritised a quiet room; the other checked breakfast timings.\nThey chose soundproof walls and a generous buffet."],[["marriage"], "The travel agent asked whether they wanted an itinerary.\nThe couple said they wanted room for surprises.\nThe agent left the afternoon blank and the family filled it in remotely."],[["marriage"], "The couple packed for a short honeymoon.\nOne suitcase held clothes; the other held chargers, medicines and documents.\nThe airline asked whether they were relocating."],[["marriage"], "The newlyweds shared a beach photograph with the family.\nAn aunt replied with nearby temples and restaurant suggestions.\nThe holiday acquired a cultural itinerary before the sunscreen dried."],[["marriage"], "The couple switched off notifications for their honeymoon.\nA cousin called to ask whether they had seen the message about switching off notifications.\nThey turned the phone on just to appreciate the irony."],[["marriage"], "At the airport, the couple found their gate had changed.\nOne checked the display; the other checked the family chat.\nThe family chat had already suggested three alternate airports."],[["marriage"], "The couple returned from their honeymoon with souvenirs.\nEvery relative requested a separate photograph and detailed review.\nThe souvenir shop had sold them a lifetime of follow-up work."],[["marriage"], "A couple agreed to save for a home after the wedding.\nThey opened a joint account and named it “future keys”.\nThe first deposit came from selling the extra wedding decorations."],[["marriage"], "The couple visited a furniture store for their new home.\nThey liked a sofa but disagreed about its colour.\nThe salesperson suggested buying two and calling it family zoning."],[["marriage"], "One spouse wanted a quiet housewarming.\nThe other invited a few neighbours and close friends.\nThe guest list expanded when the neighbours brought their relatives."],[["marriage"], "The couple wrote house rules on a fridge magnet.\nThe first rule said, “Return the remote to its place.”\nThe remote became the most carefully monitored household asset."],[["marriage"], "The couple divided the unpacking after moving.\nOne opened boxes while the other labelled shelves.\nThey found the kettle first and declared the move operational."],[["marriage"], "A relative asked whether the newlyweds had settled into married life.\nThey said they were still deciding where to keep the spare keys.\nThe relative replied, “Excellent, the important negotiations have begun.”"],[["marriage"], "The couple planned a family visit with a strict departure time.\nEveryone agreed, then offered tea just as they reached the door.\nTheir punctual exit became a three-cup project."],[["marriage"], "At their first anniversary, the couple looked through the wedding album.\nThey found 47 photos of the cake and only two of themselves eating.\nThey decided the cake had enjoyed a more documented marriage."]]);


